### PolicyFlow API Examples

@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:8000/api

### 1. Create a Policy Request (Sample from Assignment Spec)
# Travel days = 5, Age = 28 (multiplier 1.00), PLUS ($20), INTERNATIONAL (1.80), 300k (1.25)
# Expected Premium: 20 * 5 * 1.00 * 1.80 * 1.25 = ₹225.00
POST {{baseUrl}}/policy-requests
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "client_request_id": "AGT-2026-0001",
  "agent_id": "AGENT-17",
  "customer_name": "Sample Customer",
  "date_of_birth": "1998-04-10",
  "destination": "INTERNATIONAL",
  "trip_start": "2026-11-10",
  "trip_end": "2026-11-14",
  "plan_code": "PLUS",
  "sum_insured": 300000
}

### 2. Idempotency Test (Submit Same Request Again)
# Returns HTTP 200 with the existing record, no duplicate created
POST {{baseUrl}}/policy-requests
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "client_request_id": "AGT-2026-0001",
  "agent_id": "AGENT-17",
  "customer_name": "Sample Customer",
  "date_of_birth": "1998-04-10",
  "destination": "INTERNATIONAL",
  "trip_start": "2026-11-10",
  "trip_end": "2026-11-14",
  "plan_code": "PLUS",
  "sum_insured": 300000
}

### 3. List Policy Requests (with status filter and pagination)
GET {{baseUrl}}/policy-requests?status=VALIDATED&page=1
Accept: application/json

### 4. Retrieve a Specific Policy Request by ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/policy-requests/1
Accept: application/json

### 5. Submit Policy Request to Mock Insurer (Standard Flow)
POST {{baseUrl}}/policy-requests/1/submit
Accept: application/json

### 6. Reliability Scenario 1: Simulate Temporary Insurer Failure (503)
POST {{baseUrl}}/policy-requests/1/submit
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "simulation": "temporary_failure"
}

### 7. Reliability Scenario 1 Retry: Re-submit after Temporary Failure
POST {{baseUrl}}/policy-requests/1/submit
Accept: application/json

### 8. Reliability Scenario 2: Simulate Timeout during Submission (504)
POST {{baseUrl}}/policy-requests/1/submit
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "simulation": "timeout"
}

### 9. Reliability Scenario 2 Reconciliation: Check Insurer Status & Reconcile
POST {{baseUrl}}/policy-requests/1/reconcile
Accept: application/json

### 10. Webhook Callback from Mock Insurer (Confirm Policy Issuance)
POST {{baseUrl}}/mock-insurer/callback
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "provider_reference": "INS-SAMPLE-REF",
  "status": "ISSUED",
  "policy_number": "POL-20261023-XYZ101",
  "message": "Policy issued successfully"
}

### 11. Reliability Scenario 3: Duplicate Webhook Callback (Idempotent)
POST {{baseUrl}}/mock-insurer/callback
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "provider_reference": "INS-SAMPLE-REF",
  "status": "ISSUED",
  "policy_number": "POL-20261023-XYZ101",
  "message": "Policy issued successfully"
}
